#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
Nothing Liquid installer: a friendly window around the rice's install scripts,
for people new to Linux and Hyprland.

It keeps one terminal session of its own (a pseudo-terminal, so sudo asks for
the password once) and runs in it, depending on what you pick:
  - end-4's setup (dots/setup install-deps, install-setups, install-files) on a
    computer without end-4's desktop yet,
  - ./install.sh: the glass plugin and the fork's files,
  - sddm/install.sh (the login screen) and the power button setting,
  - ./uninstall.sh to take it off again.
What those scripts ask in the terminal (sudo's password, pacman's yes / no,
end-4's retry / exit / ignore after a failed command) comes up as a dialog.
Everything they print is kept in ~/.cache/nothing-liquid/logs.

  installer/nothing-liquid-installer            run it
  installer/nothing-liquid-installer --demo     stand-in steps; changes nothing
  installer/nothing-liquid-installer --dry-run  the real checks, then end-4's
                                                steps only listed and
                                                install.sh --dry-run
"""

